      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Given",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s008-given.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### Given\n\n`Given` steps are used to describe the initial context of the system - the *scene* of the scenario.\nIt is typically something that happened in the *past*.\n\nWhen Cucumber executes a `Given` step, it will configure the system to be in a well-defined state,\nsuch as creating and configuring objects or adding data to a test database.\n\nThe purpose of `Given` steps is to **put the system in a known state** before the user (or external system) starts interacting with the system (in the `When` steps).\nAvoid talking about user interaction in `Given`'s. If you were creating use cases, `Given`'",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/cucumber-2024-gherkin-reference/blocks/prose-s009-when",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "When",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s009-when.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### When\n\n`When` steps are used to describe an event, or an *action*. This can be a person interacting with the system, or it can be an event triggered by another system.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Guess a word\n- Invite a friend\n- Withdraw money\n\n{{% note \"Imagine it's 1922\" %}}\nMost software does something people could do manually (just not as efficiently).\n\nTry hard to come up with examples that don't make any assumptions about\ntechnology or user interface. Imagine it's 1922, when there were no computers.\n\nImplementation details should be hidden in the [step definitions](/docs/cucumber/step-definitions).",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/cucumber-2024-gherkin-reference/blocks/prose-s010-then",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Then",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s010-then.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### Then\n\n`Then` steps are used to describe an *expected* outcome, or result.\n\nThe [step definition](/docs/cucumber/step-definitions) of a `Then` step should use an *assertion* to\ncompare the *actual* outcome (what the system actually does) to the *expected* outcome\n(what the step says the system is supposed to do).\n\nAn outcome *should* be on an **observable** output. That is, something that comes *out* of the system (report, user interface, message), and not a behaviour deeply buried inside the system (like a record in a database).\n\nExamples:\n\n- See that the guessed word was wrong\n- Receive a",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/cucumber-2024-gherkin-reference/blocks/prose-s011-and-but",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "And, But",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s011-and-but.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### And, But\n\nIf you have successive `Given`'s or `Then`'s, you *could* write:\n\n```gherkin\nExample: Multiple Givens\n  Given one thing\n  Given another thing\n  Given yet another thing\n  When I open my eyes\n  Then I should see something\n  Then I shouldn't see something else\n```\n\nOr, you could make the example more fluidly structured by replacing the successive `Given`'s or `Then`'s with `And`'s and `But`'s:\n\n```gherkin\nExample: Multiple Givens\n  Given one thing\n  And another thing\n  And yet another thing\n  When I open my eyes\n  Then I should see something\n  But I shouldn't see something else\n```",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
